// Description: Automatic test for the MLPRO 2. 
// this is a template, it shows to the setup the scripts
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -


// [0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.


#Setup: Instructions
IMPORTANT: Warning: Avoid looking directly at any of the lights.  Protect eyes and skin from exposure to UV & IR light.
a. Enter operator initials.
b. Enter serial number.
c. Fit the ML Pro 2 to the test stand
d. Connect the USB3 cable to the PC and ML Pro 2
e. Connect the PSU to the ML PRO 2
CLICK_OK:

#1: I2C device test
CONNECT: MLPRO2
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BENUM
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEIR 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEWHITE 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEUV 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000000 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FOCUSLED 0
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat


#2: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM 

Returned result is = %BENUM%
IF: %BENUM% STR_EQ BL1,BL2,BR1,BR2,FL1,FL2,FR1,FR2,RS,RS1,RS2, //  evaulate the string aganist the Return result, give a true or false 
GOTO: #2.1: 								// if results match goto next test
TEST: FAILED // Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #3
#2.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED

#3: Range finder RIGHT side
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RRF
READLINE: MLPRO2 RRF 
Returned result is = %RRF%
IF: %RRF% <= 150 							// if result is equal to 150 or lessthan 150 the test will pass
GOTO: #3.1: 								// if results match goto next test 
Returned result is = %RRF% The expected result is =  // print this for test log information
TEST: FAILED 								// Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #4
#3.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED								// Increments PASS count and adds comment in log file


#4: Voltage check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
READLINE: MLPRO2  READVOLTS 
Returned Version is = %READVOLTS%
RANGE: %READVOLTS% 12100 50					// PASS if TEMP is between 12050 and 12150
IF:											// IF a ture result the next line below actions
GOTO: #4.1: 								// if results match goto next test
The expected result is =   between 12050 and 12150 // print this for test log information
TEST: FAILED 								// Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #20
#4.1: PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED								// Increments PASS count and adds comment in log file










































#20: Range finder RIGHT side
CHECK THAT IT READS between 120-145
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RRF
DELAY: 100
READLINE: MLPRO2 RRF
Range finder RIGHT side = %RRF%
PASS_FAIL: #20

#21: Range finder LEFT side
CHECK THAT IT READS between 120-145
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RRB
DELAY: 100
READLINE: MLPRO2 RRB
Range finder LEFT side = %RRB%
PASS_FAIL: #21

#2:INSERT THE SMALL DOMED MIRROR
a. Insert the small domed MIRROR
b. Close the flap
c. Fit the blackout cover to the ML PRO 2

DISPLAY: WIN_20230922_14_56_03_Pro.jpg
PASS_FAIL: #2

#3: Side IR
a. Check for 8 LED hot spots
IMPORTANT: You will see light reflections
b. Capture an image on the windows camera
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEIR 4095
DISPLAY: WIN_20230922_15_23_29_Pro.jpg
DELAY: 3000
PASS_FAIL: #3

#4: Side WHITE
a. Check for 8 LED hot spots
IMPORTANT: You will see light reflections
b. Capture an image on the windows camera
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEIR 0
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BSIDEWHITE 4095
DISPLAY: WIN_20230922_15_23_07_Pro.jpg
DELAY: 3000
